# Ignore everything by default
*

# -------------------------
# Keep all directories
# -------------------------
!*/

# Keep .gitkeep files anywhere
!**/.gitkeep

# -------------------------
# Allow source files anywhere
# -------------------------
!**/*.py
!**/*.cpp
!**/*.h
!**/Makefile
!**/*.tex
!**/*.bib
!**/*.md
!**/*.sh
# Sample-event dump specs (Step S1): which illustrative events ./roman should write
# full light curves for. Source, not data -- the .dat files they produce stay ignored.
!**/*.spec
!LICENSE

# -------------------------
# Ignore Python environments
# -------------------------
.roman/
.venv/
venv/
env/

# -------------------------
# Ignore Python cache
# -------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# -------------------------
# Ignore local claude files
# -------------------------
.claude/
CLAUDE.md

# -------------------------
# Ignore compiled files
# -------------------------
*.o
*.out
*.exe
*.so
*.a

# -------------------------
# Ignore build directories
# -------------------------
build/
bin/

# -------------------------
# Ignore plots/images
# -------------------------
**/*.png
**/*.jpg
**/*.jpeg
**/*.pdf
pics/**
!pics/**/.gitkeep

# -------------------------
# Ignore data files everywhere
# -------------------------
**/*.dat
**/*.fits
**/*.fit
**/*.txt
**/*.csv
**/*.h5
**/*.hdf5
**/*.npy
**/*.npz
**/*.LSST
**/*.Roman

# -------------------------
# Temporary files
# -------------------------
*.log
*.tmp
*.bak
Whitepaper/*.bbl
Whitepaper/*.blg
Whitepaper/*.log
Whitepaper/*.out
Whitepaper/*.aux
Whitepaper/*.gz
*~

# -------------------------
# Local scratch report (not part of the record)
# -------------------------
STATUS_REPORT.md

# The adopted GBTDS field centres and detector layout (Deviation 69, vendored from Penny's
# gbtds_optimizer): small, source-of-truth inputs, not generated data. Must come AFTER the
# data rules above (**/*.txt), since the last matching rule wins.
!Baseline/gbtds_layout/*

# Small static inputs ./roman and the star-list builder read, with no generator: the LSST astrometric error
# curve, Penny+2019's Roman photometric error curve, and the Pecaut & Mamajek dwarf table. Source, not
# produced data, so a fresh clone must have them (the pipeline needs them). After the **/*.txt rule.
!files/sigmaA_LSST.txt
!files/sigma_roman.txt
!CMD/empirical/EEM_dwarf_UBVIJHK_colors_Teff.txt
# The pipeline's Python requirements (after the *.txt rule, like the entries above).
!pipeline/requirements.txt
